Port osu!stable's fade-in and Hidden mod fade timings to opsu!.

Both values were explicitly marked TODO in upstream opsu!:

	fadeInTime = Math.min(375, (int) (approachTime / 2.5f));  // TODO: formula
	hiddenDecayTime = (int) (approachTime / 3.6f);             // TODO
	hiddenTimeDiff = (int) (approachTime / 3.3f);              // TODO

osu!stable fades hit objects in over 400ms, only shortening that once
the preempt time itself falls below 450ms.  At AR 9 (600ms preempt)
opsu! was fading in over 240ms instead of 400ms, so objects appeared
noticeably later and harder than in stable.

The Hidden windows are fractions of the preempt time: objects finish
fading in after 0.4 * preempt, then decay over 0.3 * preempt, leaving
them fully invisible with 0.3 * preempt still remaining.  Circle.draw
reads hiddenTimeDiff as "time remaining when fully invisible" and
hiddenDecayTime as the decay duration, so both become 0.3 * preempt.

diff --git a/src/itdelatrisu/opsu/states/Game.java b/src/itdelatrisu/opsu/states/Game.java
--- a/src/itdelatrisu/opsu/states/Game.java
+++ b/src/itdelatrisu/opsu/states/Game.java
@@ -1390,10 +1390,14 @@
 		data.calculateDifficultyMultiplier(beatmap.HPDrainRate, beatmap.circleSize, beatmap.overallDifficulty);
 
-		// hit object fade-in time (TODO: formula)
-		fadeInTime = Math.min(375, (int) (approachTime / 2.5f));
+		// hit object fade-in time
+		// osu!stable fades objects in over 400ms, shortened proportionally once
+		// the preempt time itself drops below 450ms (AR 10+ with DoubleTime).
+		fadeInTime = (int) (400f * Math.min(1f, approachTime / 450f));
 
-		// fade times ("Hidden" mod)
-		// TODO: find the actual formulas for this
-		hiddenDecayTime = (int) (approachTime / 3.6f);
-		hiddenTimeDiff = (int) (approachTime / 3.3f);
+		// fade times ("Hidden" mod)
+		// osu!stable expresses these as fractions of the preempt time: objects
+		// finish fading in after 0.4 * preempt, then decay over 0.3 * preempt,
+		// and are fully invisible with 0.3 * preempt still remaining.
+		hiddenDecayTime = (int) (approachTime * 0.3f);
+		hiddenTimeDiff = (int) (approachTime * 0.3f);
 	}
